# Optional settings for the screening console.
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) in the project folder and uncomment what you need.
# Variables already set in the environment always win over values in .env.
# Never commit a real .env file.

# --- LLM: GitHub Copilot through the VS Code proxy (vscode-copilot-proxy/) -------------------
# Optional. Leave unset: while VS Code runs the "Screening Copilot Proxy" extension, the app reads
# the token (and the port) automatically from ~/.screening-copilot-proxy.json.
# Set it only to pin a token, e.g. when the app runs under another user account. Get the value
# with the VS Code command "Screening Proxy: Copy Token" (copy it again after "Rotate Token").
# A pinned token is sent to http://127.0.0.1:5757/v1 unless the app can read a connection file
# holding the same token; when it cannot (another user account), keep the extension's port at 5757.
# COPILOT_PROXY_TOKEN=

# --- Saved runs (Run History) ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder for saved screening runs; they contain candidate personal data, so use an
# access-restricted location with backups. Default: the runs/ folder of the project.
# SCREENING_RUNS_DIR=/path/to/restricted/screening-runs

# --- Branding ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Small line of text shown above the app title (for example a team or environment name).
# Read once at startup: restart the app after changing it.
# APP_BRAND_EYEBROW=Talent Acquisition
